# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# GENERATED by gen_policy.py from its four hand-written parts. Edit those.
#
# Premise. A US management liability package for a non-profit: General Terms
# and Conditions (GTC) over four coverage sections, D&O, EPL, Fiduciary and an
# in-house counsel professional liability section (CPL). The fragment holds
# the declarations, the GTC in full and the CPL section up to clause 5. The
# other three sections appear only through their Item 6 rows.
#
# Anonymised: the insurer is "Acme Insurance Company", the insured "the Named
# Entity". Names, addresses, policy numbers, the producer, product and section
# brand names, e-mail addresses and URLs are withheld. Amounts and dates are
# the fragment's.
#
# What the mapping shows, by layer:
#
# | Layer          | Where                                                                  |
# |----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|
# | Wording        | ex:form, the declarations' variables, ex:policy-wording-v1's values    |
# | Quantification | money and date spaces, value words with placeholders, due and window ranges |
# | Party          | roles, the Named Entity from Item 1, contingent occupancies resolved per claim |
# | Eligibility    | scopes of insuring agreements and exclusions, with carve-backs negated, and two interval conditions on Item 6 dates |
# | Behaviour      | the Policy Period regime's states, triggers and transitions            |
# | Vocabulary     | the deployment's insurance activities, term classes and policy dates   |
# | Instrument     | sectioning, definitions per section, relations, qualifiers, deemings, regime |
#
# clause-map.md maps every leaf. README.md is the findings. Nothing evaluates.

